{"kind":"request","text":"Add a small, explicit Slack-like notification inbox for ephemeral chat so an addressed person can see that something new happened and open the exact thread where it happened. The current browser notices a textual `@name` only by flashing the document title while the tab is unfocused; it suppresses the first delivery, keeps no visible unread state, and gives a focused Planner session no indication at all. Temporary-message counts on individual collapsed cards are not a notification system and do not identify whether the message is for the current actor.\n\nUse the recipient-aware frames and acknowledgement model from the parent request. Add a clearly labeled Notifications affordance in the top navigation, with an accessible unread badge; do not use an unexplained bell glyph. The zero state should be quiet. Its compact popover/panel lists priority ephemeral notifications grouped by thread: direct mentions and replies to the current actor's frames, showing sender, a one-line excerpt, relative time, the durable ticket/title when the anchor is an event, and the unread count. Clicking an entry must open the exact event discussion or frame thread, scroll the first unread message into view, and mark only the messages actually revealed as read. Offer `Mark all read`, but never mark chat read merely because frames were fetched, the menu was opened, or the topic happened to render.\n\nShow the same unread marker beside the affected topic/card and in the open Thread pane so the route remains visible after the notification menu closes. New messages in the thread while it is open should clear only when they become visible. Keep notification state personal, best-effort, and isolated by room genesis plus actor fingerprint; switching identities must not share unread state. Reconcile it with the leased service acknowledgement without turning a read position into a durable event or a cross-device promise. A newly opened/switched-to actor view must surface any still-live addressed message instead of treating the first frame delivery as an automatic baseline. Self-authored frames, unrelated room chatter, stale textual names that did not resolve, and ordinary durable acts do not enter this inbox.\n\nRetain the existing unfocused-tab title knock as a secondary cue, driven by the same classifier and cleared only when the addressed item is read, not merely when the window receives focus. If a conversation expires before opening, remove the live notification honestly or show it as expired when retained in personal browser memory; never route to a different thread. Desktop/OS notifications, sounds, email, and durable notification storage are out of scope. Add focused tests for grouping, count changes, first delivery, actor switching, same-name/renamed actors, replies, thread routing, visibility-based read acknowledgement, mark-all, expiry/reset, reconnect, dedupe, and accessibility; rebuild and verify the committed UI.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-ephemeral-notifications","conditions":"A labeled accessible Notifications control has a quiet zero state and unread badge; only resolved direct mentions and replies to the current actor enter it; notifications group by exact thread and show sender/excerpt/time/anchor/count; opening routes to and scrolls the exact unread frame, while menu-open/fetch/render/focus alone do not mark it read; affected Work rows and Thread pane carry coherent unread markers; read state is isolated by genesis and fingerprint and reconciles with leased acknowledgement without durable writes; first delivery or identity switch does not hide still-live addressed chat; title knock uses the same unread classifier; expiry/reset/reconnect/dedupe/accessibility behavior is tested; OS notifications and durable storage remain out of scope; UI unit, build, embed-drift, and repository gates pass.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}